WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.429 --> 00:00:05.010
Back in the Golden Age of comic books, nobody
probably thought twice about a character's

00:00:05.010 --> 00:00:06.010
sexuality.

00:00:06.010 --> 00:00:10.800
But times change, and audiences want to find
more ways to relate to the stories they consume.

00:00:10.800 --> 00:00:14.680
Readers want to know that superheroes don't
discriminate, and creators have responded

00:00:14.680 --> 00:00:15.980
throughout the years.

00:00:15.980 --> 00:00:19.900
Here are a few superheroes who aren't afraid
to be themselves.

00:00:19.900 --> 00:00:21.020
Iceman

00:00:21.020 --> 00:00:27.119
When the X-Men were first introduced in 1963,
the team consisted of Cyclops, Beast, Angel,

00:00:27.119 --> 00:00:28.650
Marvel Girl, and Iceman.

00:00:28.650 --> 00:00:32.899
Over the years, Iceman evolved a number of
different looks and even had a few relationships.

00:00:32.899 --> 00:00:38.620
But it wasn't until a storyline in 2015 when
a time-displaced, teenage version of Iceman

00:00:38.620 --> 00:00:42.280
was introduced that psychic Jean Grey discovered
he was gay.

00:00:42.280 --> 00:00:47.050
Since the Iceman we'd all been reading since
the 1960s never indicated this was the case,

00:00:47.050 --> 00:00:49.660
except maybe once, the characters had a talk.

00:00:49.660 --> 00:00:54.510
It was revealed that Iceman couldn't cope
with being both a mutant and gay, but since

00:00:54.510 --> 00:00:58.610
he had to deal with his powers openly, he
suppressed his own sexuality to the point

00:00:58.610 --> 00:01:01.060
where he refused to even think about it.

00:01:01.060 --> 00:01:05.750
After talking with his teen self, Iceman was
able to come to terms with his feelings, and

00:01:05.750 --> 00:01:08.480
the character is now openly gay, arguably
making him Marvel's most powerful character

00:01:08.480 --> 00:01:09.480
who is also homosexual.

00:01:09.480 --> 00:01:10.480
Northstar

00:01:10.480 --> 00:01:14.360
The Canadian mutant known as Northstar is
a member of Alpha Flight and has had numerous

00:01:14.360 --> 00:01:17.080
appearances in the X-Men comics over the years.

00:01:17.080 --> 00:01:19.640
He's also Marvel's first openly gay character.

00:01:19.640 --> 00:01:24.280
In fact, in issue 51 of Astonishing X-Men,
Northstar marries his husband.

00:01:24.280 --> 00:01:28.650
Though not as popular as the X-Men, Alpha
Flight was a team of mutants who operated

00:01:28.650 --> 00:01:31.050
north of the border in Canada.

00:01:31.050 --> 00:01:35.200
Northstar serves as an integral member of
the team and has a variety of powers including

00:01:35.200 --> 00:01:40.080
superhuman speed, flight, and the ability
to fire photonic blasts of energy.

00:01:40.080 --> 00:01:45.990
He and the rest of the team were created by
legendary writer John Byrne in 1983, who at

00:01:45.990 --> 00:01:50.360
first didn't want to create the team as two-dimensional
nobodies to counter the X-Men.

00:01:50.360 --> 00:01:54.509
In order to alleviate his own misgivings,
he created more fleshed out backgrounds for

00:01:54.509 --> 00:01:58.330
the characters, which included making Northstar
a gay character.

00:01:58.330 --> 00:02:03.600
Unfortunately, Northstar's sexual orientation
could only be hinted at for years, since editorial

00:02:03.600 --> 00:02:07.810
policy at the time forbade characters from
being homosexual.

00:02:07.810 --> 00:02:08.810
Batwoman

00:02:08.810 --> 00:02:13.139
You're probably familiar with Batgirl, the
alter ego of Barbara Gordon, but Batwoman

00:02:13.139 --> 00:02:15.239
actually predates her by a few years.

00:02:15.239 --> 00:02:19.689
Ironically, she was introduced in the mid-1950s
to as a love interest for Batman, in order

00:02:19.689 --> 00:02:21.999
to counter rumors that Batman was gay.

00:02:21.999 --> 00:02:26.639
Seduction of the Innocent, a book written
by psychiatrist Fredric Wertham, had called

00:02:26.639 --> 00:02:31.599
comics into question for their influence over
children, and in particular called out the

00:02:31.599 --> 00:02:36.219
characters of Batman and Robin, suggesting
their relationship was a homosexual one.

00:02:36.219 --> 00:02:41.040
Batwoman ended up being axed as a character
midway through the 1960s only to be resurrected

00:02:41.040 --> 00:02:42.900
again in 2006.

00:02:42.900 --> 00:02:47.359
This time she was given a new twist and was
re-introduced as a gay character herself,

00:02:47.359 --> 00:02:52.169
in an effort on DC's part to offer more diverse
characters for their readers.

00:02:52.169 --> 00:02:53.689
Rictor

00:02:53.689 --> 00:02:58.329
Introduced in the late 1980s, Rictor made
his way through a number of X-titles, including

00:02:58.329 --> 00:03:01.739
X-Factor and X-Force, as well as The New Mutants.

00:03:01.739 --> 00:03:06.339
His mutant power involves generating seismic
energy, which is basically directing earthquakes

00:03:06.339 --> 00:03:08.019
at stuff.

00:03:08.019 --> 00:03:12.349
In 2009, Rictor shared a kiss with fellow
X-Force member Shatterstar, the first ever

00:03:12.349 --> 00:03:13.769
in a Marvel comic book.

00:03:13.769 --> 00:03:17.010
Since that time, the character has been an
open and out gay man.

00:03:17.010 --> 00:03:21.540
The relationship between Rictor and Shatterstar
proved to be so popular and well done that

00:03:21.540 --> 00:03:26.250
writer Peter David won a GLAAD award for the
portrayal of their relationship in the pages

00:03:26.250 --> 00:03:28.189
of X-Factor.

00:03:28.189 --> 00:03:29.249
Graymalkin

00:03:29.249 --> 00:03:33.739
Even casual Marvel fans may have heard the
word "Graymalkin" pop up now and then.

00:03:33.739 --> 00:03:37.630
It's the name of the street where Xavier's
School for Gifted Youngsters was built, as

00:03:37.630 --> 00:03:39.779
well as the name of Cable's space station.

00:03:39.779 --> 00:03:44.319
And, since 2008, Graymalkin has also been
a mutant with the young X-Men.

00:03:44.319 --> 00:03:45.480
How'd he get his name?

00:03:45.480 --> 00:03:49.389
His family owned the land on which Xavier's
school was built and the street was named

00:03:49.389 --> 00:03:50.389
after them.

00:03:50.389 --> 00:03:54.229
As it turns out, though, the character is
over 200 years old, and was caught by his

00:03:54.229 --> 00:03:57.279
father as a teen experimenting with another
boy.

00:03:57.279 --> 00:04:01.739
Enraged, his father beat him unconscious and
actually buried him alive on the land that

00:04:01.739 --> 00:04:04.049
would one day become Xavier's school.

00:04:04.049 --> 00:04:08.329
Fortunately for Graymalkin, his mutant powers
activated and saved him from death, putting

00:04:08.329 --> 00:04:12.349
him in a kind of hibernation until the present
when he was freed and eventually became a

00:04:12.349 --> 00:04:14.369
member of the Young X-Men.

00:04:14.369 --> 00:04:15.499
Anole

00:04:15.499 --> 00:04:19.540
One of the New X-Men, Anole's mutation is
a number of lizard-like abilities to match

00:04:19.540 --> 00:04:24.621
his scaly appearance, including the ability
to crawl up walls, a prehensile tongue, and

00:04:24.621 --> 00:04:26.000
adaptive camouflage.

00:04:26.000 --> 00:04:30.020
The character was introduced with hints that
he might be gay, given his closeness to his

00:04:30.020 --> 00:04:31.330
mentor Northstar.

00:04:31.330 --> 00:04:34.319
It was later confirmed as the real deal by
the comics' writers.

00:04:34.319 --> 00:04:38.610
Anole has since been praised for being openly
gay while not making every storyline revolve

00:04:38.610 --> 00:04:40.960
around that particular aspect of his life.

00:04:40.960 --> 00:04:45.120
He's gay, but he's also a superhero, so he
does superhero things that aren't affected

00:04:45.120 --> 00:04:46.120
by his sexuality.

00:04:46.120 --> 00:04:50.449
In other words, despite looking like a lizard,
he's just a normal guy.

00:04:50.449 --> 00:04:51.449
Angela

00:04:51.449 --> 00:04:55.830
One of the coolest characters in recent comics
history, Angela was originally created by

00:04:55.830 --> 00:05:00.400
Neil Gaiman and Todd McFarlane to be part
of Image Comics' Spawn universe.

00:05:00.400 --> 00:05:04.759
However, after a lawsuit over rights, a court
ordered that Angela should revert fully to

00:05:04.759 --> 00:05:07.409
Gaiman, who has since sold the character to
Marvel.

00:05:07.409 --> 00:05:11.010
Angela was originally a warrior from Heaven
sent to fight the hellspawn.

00:05:11.010 --> 00:05:15.030
Once she joined the Marvel Universe, she ended
up with the Guardians of the Galaxy, of all

00:05:15.030 --> 00:05:19.520
people, until she has to run off with Odin's
baby to protect it after finding out she,

00:05:19.520 --> 00:05:22.580
too, is an Asgardian, and the daughter of
Odin.

00:05:22.580 --> 00:05:26.610
Accompanying her is Sera, her companion, friend,
and lover.

00:05:26.610 --> 00:05:27.680
Deadpool

00:05:27.680 --> 00:05:32.340
Deadpool is played straight in his movie,
but writers and the man in red himself, Ryan

00:05:32.340 --> 00:05:37.039
Reynolds, have openly acknowledged Mr. Pool
is actually a lot more fluid in his sexuality

00:05:37.039 --> 00:05:38.039
than that.

00:05:38.039 --> 00:05:41.400
Reynolds described Deadpool as "pansexual,"
but don't take it from him.

00:05:41.400 --> 00:05:45.569
Here's Deadpool co-creator Fabian Nicieza
explaining the Merc's sexuality:

00:05:45.569 --> 00:05:47.969
"He can be hetereosexual one day.

00:05:47.969 --> 00:05:51.419
And a few days later he can believe 100 percent
that he's not."

00:05:51.419 --> 00:05:54.379
Deadpool is ready to have fun with anyone
from moment to moment.

00:05:54.379 --> 00:05:58.150
Reynolds has gone on record saying he loves
this aspect of the character and hopes that

00:05:58.150 --> 00:06:02.210
in a sequel the character could have a boyfriend,
just because it's another way Deadpool breaks

00:06:02.210 --> 00:06:04.819
the boundaries of traditional superhero roles.

00:06:04.819 --> 00:06:05.840
Thanks for watching!

00:06:05.840 --> 00:06:08.690
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:06:08.690 --> 00:06:10.740
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

